+## Geographic map and location data
+
+The geographic map uses saved shelter and rider coordinates from the selected data source. In public Judge Demo mode, these are static San Francisco fixture coordinates stored in the browser demo store. With a real Supabase session, marker positions come from the database's last-saved latitude/longitude values. The current rider-presence RPC updates heartbeat/status only; the app does not request browser geolocation or claim that rider markers are live GPS.
+
+Lines between an active rider and shelter are direct visual links, not road routes, navigation, or ETA. If either coordinate is missing or invalid, no route line is drawn. Map tiles require network access; the static PWA shell may load offline, but third-party basemap tiles are neither prefetched nor cached, and saved markers can only remain visible from the in-memory dashboard snapshot. The map shows a tile-unavailable/offline notice rather than promising offline map coverage.
+
+The default raster basemap is OpenStreetMap's standard tile service and displays visible `© OpenStreetMap contributors` attribution. It is best-effort with no availability SLA and its policy prohibits offline tile downloads. For higher-volume flood-response operations, switch `VITE_MAP_TILE_URL` and `VITE_MAP_ATTRIBUTION` together to a provider/self-hosted service with appropriate availability and explicit offline rights. See [`docs/reference/map-tiles.md`](docs/reference/map-tiles.md).
 
